THE COLLECTION\par
Acknowledgements and legal notices\par
\par
A small desktop inside The Collection\par
\par
An unofficial little desktop comedy by Atlas Reid, made in a browser with affection for familiar music software. This independent parody is not Apple software or a virtual machine and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Apple Inc.\par
\par
APPLICATION AND ORIGINAL MATERIAL\par
The application and procedural hardware are part of The Collection. Archived prototype assets include the six invented demo albums; they are no longer in the visible collection. No open-source licence has been selected for the application or its original artwork.\par
\par
INTERFACE REFERENCES\par
Apple Music and macOS inspired the familiar menus; the machinery underneath is homemade. Apple, Mac, macOS and Apple Music are trademarks of Apple Inc. This desktop has no Apple account connection, access to a real Music library, physical CD importing or subscription checkout. Its system commands stay inside this little stage set.\par
\par
PHOTOGRAPHS AND ARTWORK\par
The cliff wallpaper was supplied by the owner and resized for this prototype. No separate source-photograph licence has been established. The earlier CSS compatibility view retains supplied Razer and SuperDrive product-reference photographs; their inclusion does not imply an open-source licence.\par
\par
The SoundCloud catalogue includes Portraits by Simon Thoumire and Dave Milligan, Frieren: Beyond Journey's End (Original Soundtrack) by Evan Call, Without Fear (The Complete Edition), Sonder (2023) and I've told the trees everything by Dermot Kennedy, and Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 (Original Soundtrack) by Lorien Testard. Their public metadata snapshots and provider artwork supply the virtual albums. That artwork is third-party, all-rights-reserved material, not original demo art. Virtual disc labels are illustrative, not scans of physical CDs. No audio or streaming URLs are copied into this project. Source and provenance details are recorded in docs/ASSETS.md.\par
\par
SOUNDCLOUD\par
Real example playback uses SoundCloud's official widget and Widget API after the first-play explanation. Its branding, uploader credits and source links remain visible. Availability depends on the provider and browser. A visible widget or this acknowledgement is not separate permission from SoundCloud. The prototype's import flow saves track entries, not audio files. Flickermood by Forss is the documented widget connection example and uses the project's original disc icon.\par
\par
BANDCAMP\par
Momento by Dave Milligan (https://davemilligan.bandcamp.com/album/momento) and Still As Your Sleeping by Karine Polwart & Dave Milligan (https://karinepolwart.bandcamp.com/album/still-as-your-sleeping) use the artists' official covers and public track-metadata snapshots. The album pages mark the material all rights reserved; this credit does not grant a separate music or artwork licence. Streaming uses the visible official Bandcamp player after the first-play explanation, retaining artist and source links. Music cannot observe the player's current playback state. Import saves catalogue entries only. No Bandcamp audio or stream URLs are downloaded, copied or proxied by this project.\par
\par
THE COMPLETE SCOTTISH BAGPIPE COLLECTION\par
The 35-track catalogue and cover come from the public Apple Music album (https://music.apple.com/gb/album/the-complete-scottish-bagpipe-collection/322470599). Five same-performer title/duration matches play through SoundCloud from a different compilation: The Best of Military Bands: The King's Own Scottish Borderers Military Band (https://soundcloud.com/thekingsownscottishborderersmilitaryband/sets/the-best-of-military-bands-the). This is partial SoundCloud coverage; identical mastering is unconfirmed. Other tracks link to Apple Music. Music and artwork remain with their respective rights holders.\par
